--- !u!114 &15370536
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 15370534}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 822ea5a9b14a2a145971f1e8ee1dfdf0, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  title: 'Shift 1: Open the Session'
  concept: 'Before two applications can talk, the <b>session layer</b> sets up a
    <b>session</b>: a managed conversation with a beginning, a middle and an end.


    The
    client <b>requests</b> a session, the server <b>authenticates</b> it, both sides
    <b>negotiate</b> the rules, the server <b>confirms</b> and issues a <b>session
    ID</b>, and only then does <b>data exchange</b> begin.'
  howToPlay: 'Clients connect one at a time. Click the steps in the correct order
    to set up each session.


    Some clients will fail authentication. A session
    must never continue past a failed check, so <b>reject</b> those. Each wrong click
    costs points.'
  lesson: 'A session is set up deliberately: request, authenticate, negotiate, confirm
    (session ID), exchange data. The session ID keeps many conversations apart, and
    a failed authentication ends things before any data flows.'
  feedbackText: {fileID: 1920951046}
  clientCounterText: {fileID: 1440923727}
  clientNameText: {fileID: 1639249059}
  appText: {fileID: 1515273968}
  credentialsText: {fileID: 1865231072}
  sessionIdText: {fileID: 573757954}
  stateText: {fileID: 229035804}
  mistakesText: {fileID: 1586329735}
  logText: {fileID: 937202828}
  stepButtons:
  - {fileID: 837191569}
  - {fileID: 1822320120}
  - {fileID: 369375653}
  - {fileID: 940348539}
  - {fileID: 1069455591}
  - {fileID: 567203716}
