--- !u!114 &199905037
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 199905035}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 9fdb74de02464f749b8d94c61b14a785, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  title: 'Shift 2: Pass the Token'
  concept: 'The session layer handles <b>dialog control</b>: who may talk, and when.


    <b>Simplex</b>:
    only one side ever sends.

    <b>Half-duplex</b>: both can send, but one at
    a time.

    <b>Full-duplex</b>: both send at the same time.


    In half-duplex,
    a <b>token</b> decides whose turn it is. Only the side holding it may transmit;
    speaking out of turn causes a collision and the message must be resent.'
  howToPlay: 'Alice and Bob share a half-duplex session and messages pile up in their
    outboxes.


    Deliver <b>15 messages</b> in 50 seconds. Send from the token
    holder, and <b>pass the token</b> when the other side has a backlog. Sending
    without the token causes a collision; a full outbox drops messages.'
  lesson: Half-duplex dialog control is turn-taking enforced by a token. Whoever
    holds it talks; handing it over gives the other side the floor. Good token management
    avoids collisions without starving either side. (Full-duplex sessions don't need
    a token at all.)
  feedbackText: {fileID: 1456604158}
  duration: 50
  goal: 15
  travelTime: 0.7
  tokenPassTime: 0.4
  aliceHost: {fileID: 635968092}
  bobHost: {fileID: 1875587502}
  aliceTokenRing: {fileID: 1866895787}
